      "summary": "The Legal Aid Society reports from NYPD records that the Facial Identification Section first returned no match in a public-lewdness investigation, after which the Special Activities Unit produced a possible facial-recognition match to Trevis Williams. Legal Aid states that Williams did not match the victim's physical description but was arrested after the later match and a disputed identification procedure; it also says his life and job prospects were put on hold. CBS independently reports that Williams spent more than two days in custody, was charged with an indecent-exposure offence, and that the case was later dismissed. Williams described continuing stress and fear that he might have been required to register as a sex offender. NYPD told CBS that facial recognition was used only as a possible lead and that an arrest would not be made solely from a facial-recognition match.",
      "title": "Trevis Williams detention following facial-recognition misidentification"
